<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Wiligelmo</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">fl. c. 1099–1120</span> · Also known as Guglielmo da Modena</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Wiligelmo was a sculptor who carved the reliefs on the façade of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/modena">Modena</a> Cathedral in the early 12th century, including scenes from Genesis. An inscription praises him as worthy of honour among sculptors. His heavy, expressive figures marked a revival of monumental stone sculpture in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a> and influenced Romanesque workshops across northern Italy.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/wiligelmo.jpg" alt="Wiligelmo" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Chris Olszewski · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Modena_Cathedral_Duomo_Exterior.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
